    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1067">

                <pb facs="1428" n="1418" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/12–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-11T10:00:00+07:00">December 11,
                            1945—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 11—3:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2137. [To Consul General at Tientsin:] Please advise if situation described your
                    unnumbered December 7, 4 p.m.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d1067-f1"/> has been
                    corrected as result of our protest to Foreign Office reported Embassy’s telegram
                    2014 [<hi rendition="#italic">2114</hi>], December 7. (Sent to Tientsin,
                    repeated to Department.) Foreign Office is being informed [of] continued
                    violation of agreement with Embassy but formal protest will be delayed pending
                    reply this telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
